.Dd November 26, 2026
.Dt RETICULUM-GO-X 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm reticulum-go-x , rgox , rnx
.Nd remote command execution over Reticulum
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm reticulum-go Cm x
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl json
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Op Ar destination_hash command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Executes commands on a remote
.Nm rnx.execute
listener over an established Reticulum link. The wire format is compatible with
Python rnx.
.Sh FLAG PARSING
Before the first positional argument, all flags belong to rgox. After the first
positional argument, only multi-letter rgox flags are still parsed. Single-letter
arguments there belong to the remote command. Once remote command text begins,
every remaining argument belongs to the remote command. A literal
.Cm --
ends flag parsing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--stdout"
.It Fl config Ar path
Config file or directory. A directory uses the file named config inside it.
.It Fl p
Print the full identity hash and full destination hash, then exit. With
.Fl json ,
print one JSON object with plain hex values and no angle brackets.
.It Fl m
Mirror the remote exit code as the local exit code. Without it, client failure
codes follow the Python rnx ranges instead.
.It Fl b
Do not announce when listen mode starts.
.It Fl a Ar hash
Allowed remote identity hash. Repeatable. Bare 32-character hex and angle-bracketed
hex are accepted. Truncated hashes are rejected.
.It Fl n
Accept commands from anyone in listen mode.
.It Fl json
Emit a structured result. With
.Fl p ,
emit the machine-readable identity object.
.El
.Sh ALLOWED IDENTITIES
Listen mode reads
.Pa /etc/rnx/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.config/rnx/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.rnx/allowed_identities ,
.Pa ~/.config/rgox/allowed_identities ,
and
.Pa ~/.rgox/allowed_identities .
Each line contains one full 32-character hexadecimal identity hash. Angle brackets
are accepted. Blank lines and lines whose first non-space character is
.Cm #
are ignored. Invalid lines are skipped.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr reticulum-go 1 ,
.Xr reticulum-go-sh 1 ,
.Xr reticulum-go-cp 1
